      "polygon": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bitDvCR4reXoNBwYRr-JH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1994.655966789208,
      "y": 837.2823418665305,
      "width": 426.8551749291816,
      "height": 29.64686222762525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1010401932,
      "version": 117,
      "versionNonce": 1044503988,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514481648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is a convention baked into the Hack architecture, not something the\nhardware \"figures out.\" The definition is simply:",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is a convention baked into the Hack architecture, not something the hardware \"figures out.\" The definition is simply:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gFGOiAZ8PZX0RwfJ5wmAN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2167.9906199393195,
      "y": 880.2702920965871,
      "width": 80.18586862895818,
      "height": 14.823431113812624,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1610529844,
      "version": 117,
      "versionNonce": 1529087796,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514481648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "M  ≡  RAM[A]",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "M  ≡  RAM[A]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kkCjfyI2ZT-p_cZemYAex",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1978.2565375271881,
      "y": 901.4151514425208,
      "width": 464.54230093535546,
      "height": 44.47029334143787,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 830558476,
      "version": 146,
      "versionNonce": 1023738036,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514481648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "That is: whenever an instruction mentions M, it means \"the word in data memory\nwhose address is the current value of the A register.\" So the A register wears\ntwo hats:",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "That is: whenever an instruction mentions M, it means \"the word in data memory whose address is the current value of the A register.\" So the A register wears two hats:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WvfxTqKq4TO3d9bcffmLp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1978.4687510609106,
      "y": 951.4227614428877,
      "width": 459.22960638577615,
      "height": 14.823431113812624,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 515970484,
      "version": 117,
      "versionNonce": 2072693300,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514481648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Sometimes it holds a data value (e.g. after @5, A = 5 as a number you'll add).",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Sometimes it holds a data value (e.g. after @5, A = 5 as a number you'll add).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pl3qElA-EojFDPE-6lqW1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1978.8246004510324,
      "y": 969.5955397575212,
      "width": 463.70037637131315,
      "height": 29.64686222762525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2043367308,
      "version": 132,
      "versionNonce": 812228620,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514573742,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Sometimes it holds an address (e.g. in D=M or M=D+1, A tells memory which cell\nto read/write).",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Sometimes it holds an address (e.g. in D=M or M=D+1, A tells memory which cell to read/write).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "dCDGtWSwmuOUOcH3taIFY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1980.3510828583342,
      "y": 1018.0522975269487,
      "width": 472.6417715823177,
      "height": 59.2937244552505,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1459371828,
      "version": 183,
      "versionNonce": 1774741300,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783514607889,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The hardware doesn't distinguish these — it's the same 16 bits. It's the program\nthat decides how to use them. So the A register output naturally fans out to\naddressM: the CPU is continuously telling the outside RAM \"the address I'm\ninterested in is whatever A currently holds.\"",
      "fontSize": 11.8587448910501,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The hardware doesn't distinguish these — it's the same 16 bits. It's the program that decides how to use them. So the A register output naturally fans out to addressM: the CPU is continuously telling the outside RAM \"the address I'm interested in is whatever A currently holds.\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
