      "endArrowhead": null,
      "polygon": false
    },
    {
      "id": "m5hqNAa-2k7Al-IHcCbKM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 440.53607706606715,
      "y": 984.6354006948745,
      "width": 355.6979614199893,
      "height": 70.38454746982211,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ah",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 452166442,
      "version": 572,
      "versionNonce": 1420821418,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783694017235,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The reason why PC take A register output as the\ninput to decide where to jump is because\nthe jump target address is always whatever is\ncurrently in the A register",
      "fontSize": 14.076909493964422,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The reason why PC take A register output as the input to decide where to jump is because\nthe jump target address is always whatever is currently in the A register",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xxqGGIzVYMbpPgNXpmwOj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 306.8028830326316,
      "y": 1098.0898453829197,
      "width": 608.1469623832756,
      "height": 210.52394834527732,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ai",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1178066102,
      "version": 1101,
      "versionNonce": 537263722,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783694017235,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There's no \"jump to line 50\" that embeds the address in the jump\ninstruction itself. Instead, jumping is always a two-instruction pattern:\n\n@LOOP      // step 1: put the target address into A\nD;JGT      // step 2: if D>0, jump to the address in A\n\nThe C-instruction D;JGT has no room to hold an address — its 16 bits\nare all used up by the comp and jump fields. So it can't say where to\njump. It only decides whether to jump. The destination is implied:\n\"wherever A points.\"",
      "fontSize": 16.841915867622184,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There's no \"jump to line 50\" that embeds the address in the jump instruction itself. Instead, jumping is always a two-instruction pattern:\n\n@LOOP      // step 1: put the target address into A\nD;JGT      // step 2: if D>0, jump to the address in A\n\nThe C-instruction D;JGT has no room to hold an address — its 16 bits are all used up by the comp and jump fields. So it can't say where to jump. It only decides whether to jump. The destination is implied: \"wherever A points.\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7S4WvAYVDsg3-Ehn7oJM4",
      "type": "ellipse",
      "x": 1475.9953847797049,
      "y": 674.4268466670821,
      "width": 18.03563798996629,
