      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "am",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 412360118,
      "version": 402,
      "versionNonce": 1595990058,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783694216102,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "zr: result is zero\n\nng: result is a negative number\n\npo: we can make this to indicate that the result is a positive number -> (not(zr) and not(ng))\n\nand 3 jumps bit\n\njjj\n\nthese 3 bits indicate the jump fulfilment of the jump\n\ninstruction[0] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is positive -> jump \n\ninstruction[1] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is equal 0 -> jump \n\ninstruction[2] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is negative -> jump\n\nAnd so because it has to be a C-instruction to jump it should be\n\ninstruction[15] & ((instruction[0] & po) or (instruction[1] & zr) or (instruction[2] & ng)) -> Jump\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 10.767621834899126,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "zr: result is zero\n\nng: result is a negative number\n\npo: we can make this to indicate that the result is a positive number -> (not(zr) and not(ng))\n\nand 3 jumps bit\n\njjj\n\nthese 3 bits indicate the jump fulfilment of the jump\n\ninstruction[0] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is positive -> jump \n\ninstruction[1] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is equal 0 -> jump \n\ninstruction[2] -> if this bit is turned and ALU output is negative -> jump\n\nAnd so because it has to be a C-instruction to jump it should be\n\ninstruction[15] & ((instruction[0] & po) or (instruction[1] & zr) or (instruction[2] & ng)) -> Jump\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
